				<section class="elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-0e6b37a elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default" data-id="0e6b37a" data-element_type="section" data-e-type="section" data-settings="{&quot;ekit_has_onepagescroll_dot&quot;:&quot;yes&quot;}">
						<div class="elementor-container elementor-column-gap-default">
					<div class="elementor-column elementor-col-66 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-3c8db58" data-id="3c8db58" data-element_type="column" data-e-type="column">
			<div class="elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated">
						<div class="elementor-element elementor-element-59a6553f elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-theme-post-content" data-id="59a6553f" data-element_type="widget" data-e-type="widget" data-settings="{&quot;ekit_we_effect_on&quot;:&quot;none&quot;}" data-widget_type="theme-post-content.default">
				<div class="elementor-widget-container">
					<!--atlasvoice:start:1--><div class="tts_content_wrapper_1"><p>Stellenbosch, South Africa’s second-oldest town, blends historic charm, rolling vineyards, and dramatic mountain landscapes, making it a favourite among wine lovers and outdoor adventurers alike.</p>
<p>Just 50 minutes from the Cape Town city centre, Stellenbosch is renowned for its award-winning wine estates, quaint cafés, scenic hiking trails, and striking architecture. Here’s everything you can enjoy in Stellenbosch on your next visit:</p>
<h2>Stellenbosch Wine Tractor</h2>
<p><iframe title="wine tractor" width="640" height="480" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/D665iB1ISwY?start=13&amp;feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe></p>
<p>The Stellenbosch Wine Tractor offers a hop-on, hop-off wine-tasting experience across some of Stellenbosch’s finest wine estates. The route includes renowned estates such as Peter Falke Wines, Pink Valley Wines, Grangehurst Winery, and Alto Wine Estate. Guests can choose which vineyards to visit and explore at their own pace.</p>
<p><strong>Location:</strong> Root 44 Market, Annandale Road, Stellenbosch</p>
<p><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://www.winetractor.co.za/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.winetractor.co.za/</a></p>
<h2>Spier Wine Farm</h2>
<p><img fetchpriority="high" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="aligncenter wp-image-270276 size-full" src="https://capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/spier-wine-farm.jpg" alt="cape winelands spier wine farm" width="1000" height="500" srcset="https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/spier-wine-farm.jpg 1000w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/spier-wine-farm-300x150.jpg 300w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/spier-wine-farm-768x384.jpg 768w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/spier-wine-farm-200x100.jpg 200w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/spier-wine-farm-800x400.jpg 800w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/spier-wine-farm-600x300.jpg 600w" sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></p>
<p>Spier Wine Farm is home to South Africa’s oldest dated cellar and is set within 650 hectares of restored renosterveld and fynbos. Beyond wine tasting, it offers relaxed eateries, scenic walking routes, art installations, and local craft and design experiences, as well as curated outdoor activities such as Segway tours. The luxury hotel provides a tranquil retreat with an award-winning spa, restaurants, and, of course, acclaimed wines from the estate.</p>
<p><strong>Location:</strong> R310 Baden Powell Drive, Stellenbosch<br />
<strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://www.spier.co.za/">www.spier.co.za/</a></p>
<h2>Longridge Wine Estate<img decoding="async" class="aligncenter wp-image-308099 size-full" src="https://capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/longridge-1-2.jpg" alt="" width="1000" height="500" srcset="https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/longridge-1-2.jpg 1000w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/longridge-1-2-300x150.jpg 300w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/longridge-1-2-768x384.jpg 768w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/longridge-1-2-200x100.jpg 200w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/longridge-1-2-800x400.jpg 800w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/longridge-1-2-600x300.jpg 600w" sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></h2>
<p>Longridge Wine Estate is a pioneer in sustainable winemaking, harnessing solar energy to reduce its carbon footprint and support more efficient, environmentally conscious production. Sample the estate&#8217;s craft organic and biodynamic wines. Guests can also dine at Rykaart’s Restaurant, where a wholesome, three-course, family-style menu is inspired by seasonal produce grown on the farm. For a longer stay, the manor house offers a luxurious seven-bedroom Cape-style homestead set among working vineyards, providing an intimate escape in the heart of the estate.</p>
<p><strong>Location:</strong> Eikendal Road, Stellenbosch<br />
<strong>Website: </strong><a href="https://longridge.co.za/">longridge.co.za/</a></p>
<h2>Seven Sisters Vineyards</h2>
<p><img decoding="async" class="wp-image-308100 size-full aligncenter" src="https://capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/seven-sisters-1.jpg" alt="seven sisters" width="1000" height="500" srcset="https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/seven-sisters-1.jpg 1000w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/seven-sisters-1-300x150.jpg 300w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/seven-sisters-1-768x384.jpg 768w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/seven-sisters-1-200x100.jpg 200w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/seven-sisters-1-800x400.jpg 800w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/seven-sisters-1-600x300.jpg 600w" sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></p>
<p>Seven Sisters Vineyards is one of the first and few 100% POC-owned wine farms in Stellenbosch, founded by seven sisters. The family-run winery celebrates female empowerment and great wine in a warm, personal way. It offers an intimate tasting experience with a carefully curated menu and wine selection that complement each other. The farm also doubles as a wedding venue, with two thoughtfully designed spaces, full event coordination, and in-house catering.</p>
<p><strong>Location:</strong> Annandale Road, Stellenbosch<br />
<strong>Website:</strong> <a href="http://www.sevensisters.co.za/">www.sevensisters.co.za</a></p>
<h2>Webersburg Wine Estate</h2>
<p><img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter wp-image-308101 size-full" src="https://capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/webersberg-1.jpg" alt="Webersburg Wine Estate " width="1000" height="500" srcset="https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/webersberg-1.jpg 1000w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/webersberg-1-300x150.jpg 300w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/webersberg-1-768x384.jpg 768w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/webersberg-1-200x100.jpg 200w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/webersberg-1-800x400.jpg 800w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/webersberg-1-600x300.jpg 600w" sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></p>
<p>Webersburg Wine Estate isn’t your typical wine farm. Set against sweeping mountain scenery in Stellenbosch, the estate pairs its wines with cellar tastings and bespoke dining. Food lovers will especially enjoy the hands-on cooking experiences led by expert local chefs, which bring together South African flavours and estate-grown produce and pair them with the estate’s wines.</p>
<p><strong>Location:</strong> Annandale Road, Stellenbosch<br />
<strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://webersburg.co.za/">https://webersburg.co.za/</a></p>
<h2>Hike at Jonkershoek Nature Reserve</h2>
<p><img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter wp-image-311596 size-full" src="https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/jonkserhoek.jpg" alt="" width="1000" height="500" srcset="https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/jonkserhoek.jpg 1000w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/jonkserhoek-300x150.jpg 300w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/jonkserhoek-768x384.jpg 768w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/jonkserhoek-200x100.jpg 200w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/jonkserhoek-800x400.jpg 800w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/jonkserhoek-600x300.jpg 600w" sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></p>
<p>For nature lovers, Jonkershoek is a 9,800-hectare nature reserve featuring mountains, valleys, and streams. Well-marked hiking and mountain-biking trails traverse rugged terrain, offering everything from gentle, scenic walks along riverbanks to more demanding climbs. Set within the Cape Floral Region, one of the world’s richest biodiversity hotspots, it’s a haven for fynbos.</p>
<p><strong>Location:</strong> Jonkershoek Road, Stellenbosch</p>
<p><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://www.capenature.co.za/reserves/jonkershoek-nature-reserve">www.capenature.co.za/reserves/jonkershoek-nature-reserve</a></p>
<h2>Dylan Lewis Studio &amp; Sculpture Garden</h2>
<p><img loading="lazy" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="wp-image-308102 size-full aligncenter" src="https://capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/dylan-sculpture-museum-.jpg" alt="Dylan Lewis Studio &amp; Sculpture Garden" width="1000" height="500" srcset="https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/dylan-sculpture-museum-.jpg 1000w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/dylan-sculpture-museum--300x150.jpg 300w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/dylan-sculpture-museum--768x384.jpg 768w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/dylan-sculpture-museum--200x100.jpg 200w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/dylan-sculpture-museum--800x400.jpg 800w, https://www.capetown.travel/wp-content/uploads/dylan-sculpture-museum--600x300.jpg 600w" sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px" /></p>
<p><span style="font-size: 16px;">This sculpted indigenous garden showcases more than 60 works by South African artist Dylan Lewis. Stretching along 4km of winding paths, visitors pass through a curated outdoor gallery set within natural fynbos, dams, and mountains. After the walk, visitors can unwind at the on-site café with a warm drink by a toasty fireplace.</span></p>
<p><strong>Location:</strong> Paradyskloof Road, Paradyskloof, Stellenbosch<br />
<strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://www.dylanlewis.com/garden">www.dylanlewis.com/garden</a></p>
<h2>The Restaurant at Precious Hidden Valley</h2>
<p>Celebrating sustainability, bold African ingredients, and purposeful gastronomy, The Restaurant at Precious Hidden Valley is a must-visit for foodies. The space, co-created by Bjorn and Patrice Motsepe with Dr Precious Moloi-Motsepe, brings New African Gastronomy to life by blending ancient international techniques with a modern African vision.</p>
<p><strong>Location: </strong>Stellenbosch NU, Stellenbosch<br />
<strong>Website</strong>: <a href="https://www.hiddenvalleywines.co.za/v">www.hiddenvalleywines.co.za</a></p>
<h2>Dorp Street</h2>
<p>Dorp Street is lined with cafés, boutique shops, galleries, and guesthouses. This stretch is especially known for its heritage charm. Highlights along Dorp Street include art galleries showcasing local South African artists, wine bars pouring Stellenbosch vintages, and cosy restaurants.</p>
<h2>Related Articles</h2>
<p><a href="https://capetown.travel/your-neighbourhood-guide-to-wellington/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Your Neighbourhood Guide to Wellington</a><br />
<a href="https://capetown.travel/paarl-the-official-guide/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Explore Paarl like a Local</a><br />
<a href="https://capetown.travel/waterfall-hikes-cape-town/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Winter Hikes in Cape Town</a></p>
</div><!--atlasvoice:end:1-->				</div>
				</div>
					</div>
		</div>
